From 3eaf0cfe057231a9ba025878d3b179b0e19c7da5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:59:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v2 2/2] Input: add STMicroelectronics FTS5CU56A touchscreen
 driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add support for the ST FTS5CU56A capacitive multi-touch controller used
on the Samsung Galaxy A52 (a52q) and related devices.

The FTS5CU56A runs STMicroelectronics' sec_ts-family firmware, whose
I2C wire protocol (16-byte event FIFO read via 0x60/0x61, 0x22/0x24 ID
and firmware-version reads, 0x13 force calibration) is incompatible
with the ST reference firmware handled by the existing stmfts driver,
so it is implemented separately.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
